From 6e17872da15c39e52e5e4f7e08695eb71d95cd0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:43:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Network page: several changes with one Wi-Fi restart;
 main-network guard; RADIUS in one place

- Optional (off by default): a network created, edited or switched on is saved at once and its Wi-Fi restart waits
  for Apply now; a bar lists the waiting networks and the dashboard says so. Anything that must run at once still
  does and takes the waiting changes with it. If something else restarts Wi-Fi meanwhile, the router finishes the
  waiting networks' services by itself; with AiMesh nodes the changes stay waiting until they have been sent.
- Delete works on a main-network card again: it counts only main networks that broadcast, the Smart Connect clean-up
  runs on a main network's own Apply only, and the confirm opens in view.
- Guest networks: the "Device discovery with the main network" switch is no longer held by the AP Isolation note
  while AP Isolation is off.
- RADIUS: the main network's server is shown read-only on the RADIUS tab from the Network page's own store, so it is
  kept in one place.
- Wireless > Settings: the auto-channel options switches save and show their state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
